---
description: Rules for any code that moves, reserves or accounts for money (refund logic)
globs: app/services/**,app/workflows/**,mock_services/**
alwaysApply: false
---
- Money is integer paise. No float arithmetic, no Decimal-to-float conversions.
- Refund execution order: validate stored approval -> short transaction with
  `SELECT ... FOR UPDATE` on the order row -> reserve amount -> COMMIT -> call provider with the
  stable idempotency key -> persist result. No network call inside a DB transaction.
- Timeout or unclear provider result => status `unknown`; reconcile by querying the provider
  with the idempotency key. Never create a new key for the same operation.
- Do not trust amounts from the model or request body. Recompute from the order and rules.
- Rely on DB constraints (CHECK, UNIQUE) as the last defence, but still validate in code for
  clear errors.
- Every state change writes an audit event with a redacted payload.
- Add a concurrency test whenever reserve/execute logic changes.
